# H2c (SOFT, quad, RUN LAST): the arms that put BOTH gather streams on ONE fabric link: a trace of 24 all-gathers on the target sub-device (queue 0) and one on the drafter sub-device (queue 1) replayed together,
# both on link 0 (num_links 1: (a) sharing a link), then again at num_links 2. The first card run (2026-10-10, 'SUBDEV_H2 verdict=HANG stage=arm-shared after_s=180.0') hung the mesh at the first of these replays,
# after everything before it had worked. Why: a fabric router has ONE local-worker sender channel per link (sender channel 0, tt_metal/fabric/fabric.cpp), and a client's open writes its identity into that channel's
# single location-info block and sets the handshake word with no check that the channel is free (tt_metal/fabric/hw/inc/edm_fabric/edm_fabric_worker_adapters.hpp open_start / open_finish): two programs gathering
# over the same link overwrite each other's connection, the router acknowledges the wrong core, and the ring waits forever (the eager rounds that passed overlapped in time for a few gathers only).
# This job REPRODUCES that on purpose and measures what can still be measured: solo walls first, then the shared arms. EXPECTED: a hang (the probe's watchdog exits 3, 'SUBDEV_H2 verdict=HANG stage=arm-shared');
# READ: the line 'SUBDEV_H2 verdict=...' (HANG is the expected one); read a PASS (a different outcome) as news and repeat it once. The mesh is wedged after a hang: the ALL-BOARD RESET (Z) follows and is mandatory. Run it only after H2b.
# Duration (estimate): 25 min (one watchdog budget of 180 s, then the reset).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the sub-device overlap programme (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# the window branch (a branch that carries optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h and scripts/ci/tp4_subdev_probe.py) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the minutes.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag of the window's own image (sed -i 's/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/' *.env): this pack builds nothing, and any C2 image carries the tt-metal sub-device bindings
# it needs (the harnesses mount this checkout's files). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.

C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=subdev-shared
C2_FABRIC=FABRIC_1D
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
